[
    {
        "content": "<p>Wondering if it was possible to add more instances for Thunk?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>DecidableEq</li>\n<li>Ord</li>\n<li>Repr</li>\n<li>Hashable</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hget</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a.get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b.get</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable.isTrue</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk.ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hget</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable.isFalse</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">heq</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hget</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">heq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ord</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ord</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">compare</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordering</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">compare</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a.get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b.get</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a.get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a.get</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I was trying to lazily memoize a Thunk and required these instances, but they weren't in the standard library.<br>\nMaybe there are good reasons not to add them?</p>",
        "id": 608698124,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1783427109
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Any use of these instances will force the thunk, which raises the question why you're using a thunk in the first place, or am I misunderstanding something?</p>",
        "id": 608701122,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1783427836
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Say you have a sum type with thunks</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thunk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>You want to pass this token to function that might just look at the kind <code>Int</code> or <code>Bool</code> and not care about the value. But depending on the kind it might care and then evaluate the Thunk or place the <code>Token</code> in a map, which would require Hashable.</p>",
        "id": 608703508,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1783428441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But yes you are right, these instances would force the evaluation of the Thunk, in the case that they are used.</p>",
        "id": 608703754,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1783428511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Still I am happy with that, as long as it doesn't happen by accident, but this be double-checked when benchmarking.</p>",
        "id": 608704039,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1783428607
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think it would be a good idea to add these instances to the standard library, because I think that forcing the thunk implicitly like that is a foot gun. In the situation you described I would probably split into two types, <code>LazyToken</code> and <code>Token</code>.</p>",
        "id": 608705396,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1783428991
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>sounds reasonable, thank you</p>",
        "id": 608706541,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1783429287
    }
]